WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.642
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book three.

2
00:00:04.942 --> 00:00:08.468
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.768 --> 00:00:15.588
Unit eighteen: News and Reports. In this unit, you will report what people said and tell facts from opinions.

4
00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:17.457
News.

5
00:00:18.157 --> 00:00:21.166
News means information about things that happened recently.

6
00:00:21.466 --> 00:00:23.385
I watch the news with my dad.

7
00:00:24.085 --> 00:00:26.992
Your turn. Say: News.

8
00:00:29.692 --> 00:00:30.415
News.

9
00:00:31.417 --> 00:00:32.255
Report.

10
00:00:32.955 --> 00:00:35.686
Report means a story about an event in the news.

11
00:00:35.986 --> 00:00:38.125
The report was about the floods.

12
00:00:38.825 --> 00:00:41.373
Your turn. Say: Report.

13
00:00:44.073 --> 00:00:44.935
Report.

14
00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:46.847
Headline.

15
00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:49.848
Headline means the title of a news story.

16
00:00:50.148 --> 00:00:52.322
The headline was in big letters.

17
00:00:53.022 --> 00:00:55.837
Your turn. Say: Headline.

18
00:00:58.537 --> 00:00:59.503
Headline.

19
00:01:00.517 --> 00:01:01.367
Reporter.

20
00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:05.193
Reporter means a person who collects and tells the news.

21
00:01:05.493 --> 00:01:07.399
The reporter talked to the farmers.

22
00:01:08.099 --> 00:01:10.717
Your turn. Say: Reporter.

23
00:01:13.417 --> 00:01:14.337
Reporter.

24
00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:16.084
Fact.

25
00:01:16.784 --> 00:01:19.515
Fact means something that is true and can be checked.

26
00:01:19.815 --> 00:01:22.140
It's a fact that the Mekong is a long river.

27
00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.318
Your turn. Say: Fact.

28
00:01:28.018 --> 00:01:28.671
Fact.

29
00:01:29.683 --> 00:01:30.475
Opinion.

30
00:01:31.175 --> 00:01:33.814
Opinion means what a person thinks or believes.

31
00:01:34.114 --> 00:01:36.577
In my opinion, the film was boring.

32
00:01:37.277 --> 00:01:39.907
Your turn. Say: Opinion.

33
00:01:42.607 --> 00:01:43.550
Opinion.

34
00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:45.493
Source.

35
00:01:46.193 --> 00:01:48.285
Source means where information comes from.

36
00:01:48.585 --> 00:01:50.585
Check the source before you share news.

37
00:01:51.285 --> 00:01:53.705
Your turn. Say: Source.

38
00:01:56.405 --> 00:01:57.383
Source.

39
00:01:58.383 --> 00:01:59.036
True.

40
00:01:59.736 --> 00:02:01.503
True means correct, not false.

41
00:02:01.803 --> 00:02:03.106
Is this story true?

42
00:02:03.806 --> 00:02:06.691
Your turn. Say: True.

43
00:02:09.391 --> 00:02:10.079
True.

44
00:02:11.083 --> 00:02:13.013
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:13.313 --> 00:02:15.777
Sreypich, did you see the news today?

46
00:02:17.083 --> 00:02:20.072
Yes. The reporter said that it will rain all week.

47
00:02:21.383 --> 00:02:23.139
What else did the report say?

48
00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.949
The minister said that schools will stay open.

49
00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:30.180
Was that a fact or an opinion?

50
00:02:31.483 --> 00:02:34.252
It was a fact. I checked the source online.

51
00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:38.490
Grammar focus: Reported speech (said that).

52
00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:40.557
The reporter said that it was raining.

53
00:02:40.857 --> 00:02:45.736
In reported speech, the verb usually moves one step back: is becomes was.

54
00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:49.309
Now read and listen. Reading the News.

55
00:02:49.609 --> 00:02:52.561
Every morning, my father reads the news on his phone.

56
00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:57.637
Yesterday, a headline said that a new bridge was open in Kampong Cham.

57
00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.484
The reporter said that it would help many farmers.

58
00:03:02.783 --> 00:03:07.082
My father told me to check if a story is a fact or an opinion.

59
00:03:08.383 --> 00:03:11.265
We should always check the source to know if the news is true.

60
00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:15.214
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:15.514 --> 00:03:17.479
The reporter said blank it was raining.

62
00:03:17.779 --> 00:03:20.503
A, that. B, what. C, who.

63
00:03:24.517 --> 00:03:26.249
The answer is A: that.

64
00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:30.028
The title of a news story is the blank.

65
00:03:30.328 --> 00:03:34.492
A, headline. B, source. C, report.

66
00:03:38.483 --> 00:03:40.042
The answer is A: headline.

67
00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:43.654
Something true that can be checked is a blank.

68
00:03:43.954 --> 00:03:46.888
A, fact. B, opinion. C, story.

69
00:03:50.883 --> 00:03:52.976
The answer is A: fact.

70
00:03:54.483 --> 00:03:57.728
Now it's your turn to speak. How do you know if news is true?

71
00:04:03.028 --> 00:04:09.093
I check the source. A reporter said that some stories online are not true, so I look for facts, not opinions.

72
00:04:09.393 --> 00:04:11.161
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:16.428
Great work today! You learned eight new words and reported speech (said that).

74
00:04:16.728 --> 00:04:20.982
Today's value is truthfulness. Tell the truth and check the facts.

75
00:04:21.282 --> 00:04:24.144
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:24.444 --> 00:04:27.316
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

